WEBVTT

00:02.710 --> 00:04.820
Why are you always like this?

00:04.820 --> 00:07.320
Why do you never say anything?!

00:11.210 --> 00:12.340
Mom...

00:13.140 --> 00:14.900
Why are you crying?

00:15.430 --> 00:18.510
Tell me what's making you so sad.

00:24.960 --> 00:26.100
Dad!

00:39.670 --> 00:41.580
A dream?

00:45.830 --> 00:49.640
It's back, huh? I haven't had that dream 
since I started high school.

00:54.120 --> 00:55.660
MOM: LAST TRAIN, I THINK

SORRY

(TODAY)

AT WORK

00:54.120 --> 00:55.660
GOT IT

00:56.160 --> 01:00.620
I have a pretty good idea 
why I had that dream again.

01:01.100 --> 01:05.090
Because I don't like you...

01:09.520 --> 01:11.880
I love you.

01:14.160 --> 01:16.080
I love Umi, too.

01:16.660 --> 01:20.480
I'd like to let her know 
right away... if I could.

01:22.020 --> 01:26.650
But I know people can 
fall out of love just as easily.

01:27.040 --> 01:29.250
I've seen it first-hand.

01:30.220 --> 01:32.720
It made me really happy 
when she said she loved me.

01:33.510 --> 01:37.410
But I'm not a good fit for Umi right now.

01:40.580 --> 01:43.040
IT'S BEDTIME. GOODNIGHT

(TODAY)

MORNING, MAKI

01:40.580 --> 01:43.040
NIGHT

01:41.580 --> 01:43.040
LET'S WALK TO SCHOOL
TOGETHER

01:43.040 --> 01:44.150
I'll try my best, though.

01:44.950 --> 01:47.640
I want to be able to say 
Asanagi Umi's my girlfriend,

01:48.470 --> 01:50.980
and I want to become a guy 
who can say it loud and proud.

03:24.950 --> 03:26.390
Interesting.

03:26.390 --> 03:29.820
So you want to put off your reply 
to my declaration of love...

03:29.820 --> 03:32.730
and keep me open 
as a backup option, right?

03:32.730 --> 03:34.740
W-Wrong!

03:35.840 --> 03:39.920
Actually, I guess I can see 
why it'd come off that way.

03:40.470 --> 03:41.240
Sorry.

03:41.240 --> 03:43.070
You should be.

03:43.070 --> 03:48.010
But I know I'm clearly 
your number-one choice.

03:49.380 --> 03:52.250
So I won't tell you off any more.

03:52.500 --> 03:56.510
You're lucky I'm such a sweet, 
understanding girl.

03:56.510 --> 03:59.970
If it were anyone else, your ass would be 
three feet in the ground right now.

04:01.350 --> 04:02.930
Right.

04:03.760 --> 04:06.230
C'mon, get it together.

04:06.230 --> 04:09.240
You're gonna become a guy 
worthy of me, remember?

04:09.240 --> 04:10.040
Yeah.

04:10.440 --> 04:11.770
Hey, Maki...

04:12.070 --> 04:14.190
Your lips are really cracked.

04:14.540 --> 04:17.650
Hang on. I'll put some 
of my lip balm on you.

04:20.680 --> 04:23.580
Okay, that should do it.

04:23.900 --> 04:30.930
Hey, uh, isn't that lip balm 
the one you use every day?

04:30.930 --> 04:32.490
Well, yeah.

04:33.470 --> 04:34.800
Oho?

04:34.800 --> 04:39.770
What's this, Maki-kun, my boy? 
Indirect kiss on your mind, maybe?

04:40.530 --> 04:43.430
I-I mean, yeah?

04:43.700 --> 04:47.270
It doesn't bother me. After all...

04:47.270 --> 04:50.600
I used a brand-new stick on you.

04:51.150 --> 04:53.880
You can keep this.

04:53.880 --> 04:56.900
Use it and take better care of your lips.

04:57.240 --> 04:58.200
Got that?

04:58.870 --> 05:01.360
Yeah, yeah, I got you.

05:03.000 --> 05:04.500
Hey, Maki...

05:04.500 --> 05:05.960
What now?

05:06.580 --> 05:11.540
We can use the same lip balm when 
we've made some more progress, okay?

05:16.590 --> 05:18.510
Morning, Umi!

05:18.510 --> 05:20.810
Yeah, yeah, morning.

05:21.240 --> 05:23.760
Morning to you too, class rep.

05:23.760 --> 05:26.640
Uh, Nitta-san?

05:26.640 --> 05:29.970
By "class rep," do you mean me?

05:29.970 --> 05:34.830
Yep. You repped our class in 
the school fest's committee, so class rep.

05:34.830 --> 05:35.900
Pretty obvious.

05:35.900 --> 05:38.610
I don't think so, actually.

05:39.330 --> 05:43.030
By the way, our class's display 
proved quite popular,

05:43.030 --> 05:46.620
SPECIAL PRIZE

05:43.830 --> 05:46.160
and we received a special prize for it.

05:46.620 --> 05:49.500
Anyway, let's not get nitpicky.

05:49.930 --> 05:52.250
So, class rep...

05:52.500 --> 05:54.840
Are you and Asanagi really dating?

05:56.350 --> 05:58.710
Nina?

05:58.710 --> 06:02.380
Wait, that was merely a joke. A jest.

06:02.380 --> 06:05.150
So please don't put me in the iron claw...

06:07.850 --> 06:10.640
I'm tapping out, Asanagi!

06:11.910 --> 06:13.080
Sheesh.

06:18.390 --> 06:20.010
Do you have something to say, too?

06:20.010 --> 06:21.610
Oh, nah.

06:22.000 --> 06:25.130
It's just, you're being awfully 
awkward around Maki-kun.

06:25.130 --> 06:26.320
Did something happen?

06:26.660 --> 06:29.660
Wh-What? Nothing happened!

06:29.660 --> 06:34.540
Wow, what's gotten into you? 
You're red as a tomato.

06:34.540 --> 06:37.860
B-Beats me. Must be the heater's fault.

06:38.380 --> 06:40.410
You're adorable, Umi.

06:42.550 --> 07:03.570
MAEHARA

06:43.120 --> 06:47.160
I know this is sudden, 
but Christmas Eve's coming up...

06:48.130 --> 06:49.310
You sleaze.

06:49.310 --> 06:50.310
What?

06:50.310 --> 06:52.020
Where'd that come from?!

06:52.020 --> 06:57.270
I mean, you're inviting me to spend 
Christmas at your place, aren't you?

06:57.270 --> 06:59.320
Well, yeah.

06:59.990 --> 07:02.560
Do you already have plans or something?

07:04.070 --> 07:13.160
MAEHARA

07:16.070 --> 07:20.140
Sorry. I've got plans on Christmas Eve.

07:20.140 --> 07:23.170
No!

07:24.650 --> 07:26.840
Hey, if you're okay with it,

07:26.840 --> 07:29.640
could you be my date 
to the Christmas party?

07:29.640 --> 07:33.860
I'm sorry. I'm going 
to the party with friends,

07:33.860 --> 07:35.310
and also...

07:35.560 --> 07:40.020
Uh, I-I have somebody I like.

07:40.020 --> 07:42.300
We should go over there now.

07:42.300 --> 07:44.880
Huh? She'd find out we were watching.

07:44.880 --> 07:47.570
It's okay. Yuu already knows.

07:47.570 --> 07:52.780
You know a rejection won't turn 
messy if friends show up after.

07:52.780 --> 07:53.660
I see.

07:52.780 --> 07:54.200
Yuu-chin!

07:55.180 --> 07:57.170
Christmas party, huh?

07:57.960 --> 08:08.090
COMBINED HIGH SCHOOL CHRISTMAS PARTY

07:58.820 --> 08:00.530
According to Umi,

08:00.530 --> 08:03.980
they're renting out a part of the 
local civic center on Christmas Eve

08:03.980 --> 08:07.710
to host a party in collaboration 
with other high schools in the area.

08:08.090 --> 08:12.800
ABOUT THE CHRISTMAS PARTY

08:08.090 --> 08:12.490
The deadline to sign up for it 
was at the start of the second term.

08:13.070 --> 08:16.180
I wasn't friends with Umi
 yet at that point,

08:16.180 --> 08:19.650
and I ignored the whole thing, 
thinking it had nothing to do with me.

08:20.500 --> 08:24.840
Looking back, 
that was a really stupid decision.

08:25.880 --> 08:27.610
What? That's too bad!

08:27.610 --> 08:30.840
I wish you were still able 
to sign up, Maki-kun.

08:30.840 --> 08:33.990
This one's totally on me 
for not thinking it through.

08:33.990 --> 08:36.110
You three go have fun.

08:36.110 --> 08:38.330
Whoa, whoa!

08:38.330 --> 08:41.220
Don't jump to conclusions, class rep.

08:42.710 --> 08:46.660
I won't be with our 
dynamic duo for the party.

08:46.660 --> 08:48.740
You're not coming with us, Ninacchi?

08:48.740 --> 08:51.640
And "dynamic duo"?

08:52.020 --> 08:54.850
I'll be going with my boyfriend!

08:55.140 --> 08:58.730
An upperclassman asked me out 
during the school festival.

08:58.730 --> 09:00.800
What? That's news to me!

09:00.800 --> 09:02.150
What the heck?!

09:02.930 --> 09:04.610
Wanna know the deets? Do you?

09:04.610 --> 09:05.710
Not particularly!

09:05.710 --> 09:06.690
Hey!

09:06.690 --> 09:08.180
You wanna know, right, class rep?

09:08.180 --> 09:09.780
I, uh...

09:15.790 --> 09:20.540
Maehara, I'll ask just in case. 
You know who I am, right?

09:20.540 --> 09:24.310
Well, yeah, we're classmates.

09:24.310 --> 09:25.690
Seki-kun.

09:26.090 --> 09:30.400
He said he wanted to talk to me 
and dragged me out here.

09:30.400 --> 09:33.920
Is this the "getting shaken down 
for money" I've heard so much about?

09:35.270 --> 09:38.310
I'll cut right to the chase.

09:38.310 --> 09:39.680
O-Okay.

09:41.750 --> 09:45.490
I need some advice with Amami-san!

09:46.590 --> 09:47.440
Huh?

09:47.900 --> 09:51.240
BASEBALL TEAM

09:48.630 --> 09:51.240
I'm all baseball, all the time.

09:51.600 --> 09:54.870
Until I joined high school, 
I was never interested in girls.

09:55.200 --> 09:58.120
But the moment I saw Amami-san 
at the entrance ceremony,

09:58.120 --> 10:01.200
it felt like I was struck by lightning.

10:02.110 --> 10:06.290
At first, I was content just getting 
glimpses of her from afar.

10:06.550 --> 10:09.340
But it's December now, you know?

10:09.340 --> 10:11.720
We'll be second-years in four months,

10:11.720 --> 10:14.840
and I might not even end up 
in the same class as her.

10:15.890 --> 10:19.720
I don't like being roundabout, 
so I'll ask straight up.

10:20.100 --> 10:23.230
Maehara, please be friends with me!

10:23.230 --> 10:28.150
And I'd like you to ask Asanagi 
to introduce me to Amami-san!

10:28.510 --> 10:34.770
Invite me to join your group 
at the Christmas party as your friend!

10:38.190 --> 10:39.040
Sorry.

10:40.300 --> 10:43.620
If that's what this is about, 
I'll have to turn you down.

10:45.030 --> 10:49.470
Anything else? Are we done?

10:49.470 --> 10:50.940
Ugh.

10:51.340 --> 10:53.710
That makes sense.

10:53.710 --> 10:58.850
I showed up asking all this when 
I've never even talked to you before.

10:58.850 --> 11:01.540
I must've come off as a total asswipe.

11:01.540 --> 11:03.040
I wouldn't say that.

11:03.750 --> 11:06.650
I'm sorry I couldn't help.

11:06.650 --> 11:09.920
I'm sorry for suddenly 
dragging you out here, too.

11:10.380 --> 11:12.980
Thanks for hearing me out, man.

11:13.460 --> 11:17.040
Also, you usually look so meek,

11:17.040 --> 11:19.570
but you know how to say no, huh?

11:19.570 --> 11:21.950
I've gained some respect for you.

11:22.970 --> 11:24.160
Yeah?

11:24.850 --> 11:30.820
But I'm not nearly as cool 
as someone else I know.

11:33.860 --> 11:38.100
Personally, I'm a bit iffy 
on the Christmas party.

11:38.100 --> 11:39.050
Why's that?

11:39.340 --> 11:41.560
Because one of 
the participating schools...

11:41.560 --> 11:43.160
is Tachibana Girls'.

11:43.160 --> 11:44.520
Ah.

11:44.520 --> 11:49.140
I didn't know it was going to end up 
like this when I signed up for it.

11:49.140 --> 11:53.230
Yeah, it'd be kinda awkward 
if you ran into them there.

11:53.230 --> 11:56.060
But I've already paid for my ticket.

11:56.060 --> 11:59.370
I'll just eat all the food 
and head straight out.

11:59.990 --> 12:01.940
Oh, but...

12:02.940 --> 12:07.650
the party will end around 
8 or 9 PM, probably.

12:07.650 --> 12:12.000
So, uh, you see what I'm getting at?

12:12.680 --> 12:16.900
Sure. I'll get some light snacks 
and wait for you.

12:16.900 --> 12:17.910
Thanks!

12:22.750 --> 12:26.180
It's not every day I see you 
smoking at home, Mom.

12:27.100 --> 12:29.140
Sorry about that.

12:29.530 --> 12:33.180
It's fine. Work been busy?

12:33.180 --> 12:34.900
This year in particular.

12:35.260 --> 12:39.250
But still, it's a lot better than 
last year in many ways.

12:39.250 --> 12:42.870
Hey, that stuff's in the past now.

12:43.680 --> 12:51.000
The last time Mom smoked in front 
of me was just around a year ago.

12:52.090 --> 12:55.190
It was right in the middle of her 
divorce proceedings with Dad.

12:56.520 --> 12:59.840
Hey, Mom? Are you... okay?

13:00.200 --> 13:01.280
You're not pushing yourself?

13:02.930 --> 13:07.180
I'm totally fine. It is getting tougher 
on my body as I grow older,

13:07.440 --> 13:09.920
but mentally, I've got room to spare.

13:09.920 --> 13:12.900
Yeah? Glad to hear it.

13:14.190 --> 13:17.240
Anyway, on the night of the 24th...

13:19.580 --> 13:23.070
Can I really come to your 
Christmas party, too?!

13:23.420 --> 13:26.400
We're meeting up at your place 
on the night of the 24th, right?

13:27.800 --> 13:29.140
Sorry, Yuu.

13:29.140 --> 13:34.330
I've got other plans after the party. 
I don't think I can go home with you.

13:34.330 --> 13:36.600
Huh? Plans at night?

13:36.600 --> 13:39.960
Yeah, so try to find someone 
to walk with you...

13:39.960 --> 13:41.380
Is it Maki-kun?

13:42.630 --> 13:44.270
You two are so lovey-dovey.

13:44.270 --> 13:46.350
I told you, we're not together yet!

13:46.350 --> 13:47.500
"Yet"?

13:49.890 --> 13:52.500
But you're meeting up on Christmas Eve.

13:52.500 --> 13:54.310
It's not what you think, really!

13:54.310 --> 13:57.700
It's perfectly normal to have 
a Christmas thing with friends.

13:57.700 --> 14:01.490
Heck, you could come, too! Yeah!

14:03.230 --> 14:06.090
And here we are.

14:08.200 --> 14:10.760
What is this emotion 
I'm feeling right now?

14:12.990 --> 14:14.710
A... Amami-san!

14:15.290 --> 14:20.300
Uh, I'd like to speak 
to you alone. Do you mind?

14:20.300 --> 14:25.040
Huh? Oh... Okay, I guess?

14:28.140 --> 14:30.430
Aren't you going to go, Nina?

14:30.430 --> 14:32.890
I do wanna see how it plays out.

14:32.890 --> 14:34.440
There's only one thing it could be!

14:33.220 --> 14:37.250
But most of us already knew 
that Seki had a thing for Yuu-chin,

14:34.440 --> 14:35.670
It has to be that!

14:35.670 --> 14:37.750
Good luck, Seki-kun!

14:37.250 --> 14:40.610
and it's obvious what her answer 
will be, so it's whatever.

14:37.750 --> 14:40.610
But I heard she turned an upperclassman 
down just the other day.

14:41.000 --> 14:44.880
Now, if this had been our class rep, 
it'd be a whole different kettle of—

14:45.530 --> 14:49.220
Wait, Umi-san! I was just kidding!

14:49.590 --> 14:50.990
For crying out loud!

15:09.330 --> 15:11.430
Man, that was funny.

15:11.970 --> 15:15.690
Nozomu actually asked 
Amami-san out for real.

15:16.240 --> 15:21.290
Eh, we can give him company on 
Christmas Eve. Show him he's still got us.

15:21.650 --> 15:23.360
What, us and our girlfriends?

15:23.360 --> 15:25.900
I'm gonna go talk to Yuu.

15:25.900 --> 15:31.500
Wait, didn't he say he hung out with 
girls a bunch during middle school?

15:28.110 --> 15:31.160
Class rep, go talk to Seki.

15:31.160 --> 15:34.310
Staying here will only corrupt you.

15:31.500 --> 15:32.820
Musta been lying.

15:32.820 --> 15:37.320
If he was used to female company, 
he wouldn't pull what he just pulled.

15:34.310 --> 15:36.080
I will. How about you?

15:36.470 --> 15:40.050
Hey, I practically grew up 
around these parts.

15:44.950 --> 15:47.130
You rushed things, Seki-kun.

15:48.010 --> 15:51.240
I really messed up, huh?

15:52.830 --> 15:55.880
What were the people in class 
saying about me?

15:55.880 --> 16:00.520
There was lots of talk, 
but it was all in an alien language.

16:00.520 --> 16:03.150
And I lacked the brainpower 
to translate it.

16:05.080 --> 16:07.350
Damn, you can be surprisingly nasty.

16:07.350 --> 16:08.990
And good at trash talk, to boot.

16:09.480 --> 16:12.950
You can't assume that all quiet people 
have agreeable personalities.

16:17.110 --> 16:19.280
So, Seki-kun...

16:21.260 --> 16:25.030
Since you've been rejected by Amami-san, 
what are you going to do now?

16:25.830 --> 16:28.490
What should I do, huh?

16:28.990 --> 16:34.900
Common sense says I should just forget 
about her and try to find a new love...

16:34.900 --> 16:37.810
But it's never that easy, is it?

16:40.020 --> 16:42.410
Lucky you.

16:42.410 --> 16:44.270
You're dating Asanagi, right?

16:44.270 --> 16:45.290
Urk.

16:46.150 --> 16:51.360
Actually, we're technically 
not dating yet.

16:52.160 --> 16:52.840
Wha?

16:54.460 --> 16:56.290
I get it now.

16:56.630 --> 17:01.280
Hey, I can't talk, given my 
total lack of dating experience,

17:02.150 --> 17:04.900
but you should make things 
official as soon as possible.

17:04.900 --> 17:08.680
Asanagi's been making a comeback 
with the guys lately.

17:08.680 --> 17:10.510
What? Really?

17:10.510 --> 17:17.100
Yeah, they're saying she's been looking 
mellower and prettier since the fest.

17:17.100 --> 17:21.370
Guys from other classes 
jokingly ask me to hook them up.

17:21.370 --> 17:23.460
O-Oh, yeah?

17:23.900 --> 17:28.640
Anyway, just be careful some other guy 
doesn't steal her from you.

17:28.640 --> 17:32.820
That's all the advice 
I can give you as your bro.

17:33.180 --> 17:36.830
I appreciate it. Wait, huh?

17:37.290 --> 17:39.120
"Bro"?

17:39.120 --> 17:44.790
Yeah, I figured we were cool. 
We seem to be on similar wavelengths.

17:45.190 --> 17:47.510
Would you rather not?

17:47.510 --> 17:49.820
Oh, that's not it.

17:49.820 --> 17:55.550
It's just, are you sure I deserve
 your trust when we've barely talked?

17:56.030 --> 18:01.240
It's not that big a deal. 
You overthink things too much, man.

18:01.240 --> 18:02.140
I know.

18:02.420 --> 18:04.310
If it's all right with you, then,

18:05.000 --> 18:08.610
let's be friends from now, Seki-kun.

18:08.610 --> 18:10.990
Sure. Let's do this,

18:11.390 --> 18:12.280
Maki.

18:13.150 --> 18:14.150
Yeah, let's...

18:14.920 --> 18:18.500
Er, N-Nozomu.

18:20.940 --> 18:22.410
Morning, Maki.

18:22.410 --> 18:25.250
It's awfully cold today.

18:25.990 --> 18:27.730
I'd like some coffee.

18:29.390 --> 18:32.800
I never expected you 
and Seki to become friends.

18:33.390 --> 18:37.760
I thought you two lived in different 
worlds and would never jive.

18:37.760 --> 18:42.100
Just goes to show, you never 
know until you talk to them.

18:43.260 --> 18:45.540
Either way, I'm happy for you.

18:49.660 --> 18:52.360
You should make things official 
as soon as possible.

18:54.190 --> 18:57.120
H-Hey, Umi?

18:57.390 --> 18:58.690
Hm?

18:58.690 --> 19:00.960
This weekend...

19:02.110 --> 19:06.300
Do you wanna go catch a movie with me?

19:06.300 --> 19:10.580
Wait, are you asking me on a date?

19:11.460 --> 19:13.340
Something like that.

19:13.820 --> 19:18.800
We've always hung out on Fridays, 
but never over the weekend.

19:19.050 --> 19:22.610
So I figured we could 
do that for a change.

19:25.970 --> 19:27.940
Let's go on that date.

19:29.400 --> 19:32.810
Oh, but if we're doing it on Saturday,

19:32.810 --> 19:36.360
I want you to come with me 
somewhere after school on Friday.

19:37.190 --> 19:40.620
That's fine by me, but where are we going?

19:41.070 --> 19:44.580
If we're going on a date, 
you need the right outfit for it!

19:45.700 --> 19:46.590
Huh?

19:46.590 --> 19:51.050
Wait, were you planning to make do 
with the clothes you already have?

19:51.850 --> 19:53.030
I can't?

19:53.030 --> 19:53.970
You can't!

19:53.970 --> 19:55.170
They do the job—

19:55.170 --> 19:56.750
You. Can. Not!

19:56.750 --> 19:57.710
Yes, ma'am.

19:59.440 --> 20:02.810
And so the rest of the week passed,

20:02.810 --> 20:04.560
and Friday was upon us.

20:05.190 --> 20:07.620
We're checking out thrift stores first?

20:07.620 --> 20:10.680
Yeah. Stick close to me, you two.

20:10.680 --> 20:11.730
Roger!

20:14.360 --> 20:17.730
Whoa, it's so crowded.

20:19.990 --> 20:21.030
Whoa!

20:22.490 --> 20:24.380
Are you okay, Amami-san?

20:24.380 --> 20:27.030
Oh, yeah. Sorry about that.

20:28.450 --> 20:31.880
Your hand's pretty rugged, Maki-kun.

20:31.880 --> 20:34.210
That's such a boy thing.

20:34.210 --> 20:39.300
You think? It's probably nothing 
compared to the guys who play sports.

20:40.000 --> 20:42.640
Wrap it up, you two.

20:43.790 --> 20:46.520
Sorry, Maki-kun! I wasn't thinking.

20:46.820 --> 20:48.900
Nah, me neither.

20:50.430 --> 20:52.940
Hey, I'm sorry, Umi.

20:52.940 --> 20:55.400
Don't be. I'm not mad.

21:00.190 --> 21:01.160
What?

21:01.730 --> 21:04.120
I don't want to lose you in this crowd.

21:04.390 --> 21:05.470
So I thought...

21:07.480 --> 21:08.540
Fine.

21:08.830 --> 21:10.420
If you insist.

21:13.250 --> 21:16.210
Uh, Umi-san?

21:17.060 --> 21:18.420
Quiet, you.

21:23.320 --> 21:25.850
I-I'm beat.

21:40.030 --> 21:44.820
ASANAGI: LET'S WALK TO
SCHOOL TOGETHER


YUU AND I ARE WAITING
BY THE GATE

21:40.030 --> 21:44.820
GOT IT. I'LL BE RIGHT THERE

21:40.520 --> 21:43.240
Look forward to tomorrow.

21:43.240 --> 21:45.950
I'll dress up and look 
super pretty for you!

21:51.930 --> 21:53.750
I-I'm so sorry!

21:54.170 --> 21:56.790
Oh, look who we have here.

21:59.230 --> 22:01.640
It's been a while, Maki.

22:02.840 --> 22:04.090
Dad?

